$\therefore$ Required equation of circle is \begin{array}{l}
(x \pm 2)^{2}+(y \pm 4)^{2}=20 \\
\Rightarrow x^{2}+y^{2} \pm 4 x \pm 8 y=0
\end{array}

Let $r$ be the radius of the circle.
<img src="/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fap_eamcet%252FFZTzAGTTAQXaEUL8h2ZVtaGvRYbK-HUYUi7tnYHDtnI.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2" data-qx-orig-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fap_eamcet%2FFZTzAGTTAQXaEUL8h2ZVtaGvRYbK-HUYUi7tnYHDtnI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media" data-qx-storage-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fap_eamcet%2FFZTzAGTTAQXaEUL8h2ZVtaGvRYbK-HUYUi7tnYHDtnI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media"><br>
Now, perpendicular distance $\begin{aligned} A C \text{ and } =\frac{|2+4+2|}{\sqrt{1^2+1^2}}=\frac{8}{\sqrt{2}}\\ \text{ and } =4 \sqrt{2}
\end{aligned}$ In right angled $\triangle C A B, \begin{aligned}$ r² & =(A C)^2+(A B)^2 \\
& =(4 $\sqrt{2})^2+(3)^2=32+9 \\
\Rightarrow \quad r²  \text{$ and $}  =41 \Rightarrow$r=\sqrt{41}
\end{aligned}

$(r+1)^2=\alpha^2+9$
